Reference quirk. The source has `\rem`, `\h` and `\mt1` on three lines, all
empty. Paratext writes the two markers after the empty `\rem` as its text,
`<para style="rem">\h\mt1</para>`, which no reading of USFM supports. The
parser gives each marker its own empty paragraph.

--- origin.xml
+++ origin.xml
@@ -1,7 +1,9 @@
 <usx version="3.0">
   <book code="GEN" style="id" />
   <para style="ide" />
-  <para style="rem">\h\mt1</para>
+  <para style="rem" />
+  <para style="h" />
+  <para style="mt1" />
   <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="GEN 1" />
   <para style="s1" />
   <para style="m">
